# snake-drive.pdl - from ANY editor state to a STARTED Snake real time game with YOU as seat p1, then steer right. UNTESTED LIVE when generated: run it once with the real window, fix the labels, then delete this line.
# Run: RELAY_DRIVE_NO_ESC=1 relay_drive <editor window pid> run @.apps/snake/tests/snake-drive.pdl <x window id>
# Pause = Player > Stop: the driver stops asking for ticks and writes no row. STEP fields split on a bar, so an expectation holds no bar.
STEP | in | off
STEP | ensure | pm-play | tb-player
STEP | tapid | pm-play
STEP | sleep | 3000
STEP | expect | @.apps/rpg-edit-hq/state/game_ui.txt | contains | players, then START | 15
STEP | press | label:you play
STEP | press | label:START GAME
STEP | expect | @.apps/rpg-edit-hq/state/game_ui.txt | contains | tick | 20
STEP | see | label:Right
STEP | press | label:Right
STEP | expect | @.apps/rpg-edit-hq/state/games/snake/game/ledger.txt | contains | EVENT | 10
